# netsurf: UTF-8/Latin-1/ASCII conversions without iconv (forms submit)
# Generated 2026-09-24
#
# Hardware runs 15 and 16: interaction step 18 (submit IN-form) failed on
# the device only. The engine log says why: "fetch_data_list_add: Could not
# encode name for fetch data" -- form names and values are converted to
# the form's charset ("UTF-8//TRANSLIT") by utf8_to_enc, i.e. iconv, and
# the Vita's newlib iconv has no converters at all (hardware run 2 found
# the same for the parser). The simulator uses glibc's iconv, so it
# passed there. utf8_convert now does UTF-8 <-> UTF-8, Latin-1 /
# Windows-1252 and ASCII itself (unmappable characters become '?') and
# leaves only other charsets to iconv. Step 19 failed as a consequence
# (the caret stayed in the field).

